From 90f5acb726935738cb3d664ab1ff97e7309a7a75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:31:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 261/277] Assembly in the integrated environment: STEP parts,
 joints by how they move

- "Open file" in the panel that puts parts takes STEP and IGES files (read
  into a document of their own, copied into the assembly when put)
- Two round faces picked on two parts of an assembly offer "Insert (turns
  and slides)", "Hinge (turns only)" and "Join rigidly" next to them; the
  joints are named by how the parts move. The bar also works in an active
  assembly (which counts as being edited)
- The design check does not call a pin in a hole with a clearance fit (same
  axis, up to 0.5 mm) floating
- The sample STEP files of the first steps have a 12 mm hole and an 11.8 mm pin

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
